#summary Macro map: the area overview no longer overlaps feature tiles mid-zoom
#describe what The Macro map no longer draws an area's overview text on top of its header and feature tiles while zooming.
#describe before Between the Overview and Features zoom levels the area name, purpose and counts overlapped the tiles.
#describe after The overview fades out completely before the header and the feature tiles fade in.
#describe verified Reproduced the overlap by zooming out from an entered area and checked it is gone; macro e2e (41), typecheck, lint and the lod unit tests are green.
~ src/renderer/lib/macroview/lod.ts
~ src/renderer/lib/macroview/paint.ts
~ test/macroview-lod.test.ts
#order src/renderer/lib/macroview/lod.ts
#order src/renderer/lib/macroview/paint.ts
#order test/macroview-lod.test.ts
#reason src/renderer/lib/macroview/lod.ts Adds one hand-off point so the area overview and the feature detail never show together
#reason src/renderer/lib/macroview/paint.ts Fades the overview and the header with tiles through the shared hand-off instead of two overlapping ramps
#reason test/macroview-lod.test.ts Pins that the overview and the detail are never both visible at any zoom weight
#story Zooming the Macro map
#step actor Reviewer
#step action zooms the map in or out between areas and features
#file src/renderer/lib/macroview/paint.ts
#step subject an area on the Macro map
#file src/renderer/lib/macroview/lod.ts
#below interaction can read each area while it changes level
